# Generated from: specs/21-support-policy-based-self-scheduling-and-recurring-service-commitments/requirements.md
Feature: Support policy-based self-scheduling and recurring service commitments
  As a volunteer
  I want to claim either one opening or an ongoing service cadence under the group's scheduling policy
  So that regular service does not require repeating the same request every week

  @SCN001
  Scenario Outline: Persisted policy controls the public outcome
    Given a published opening uses <policy>
    When a volunteer reviews and submits the labelled form
    Then the page explains <consequence> before submission
    And the authoritative result is <result>

    Examples:
      | policy           | consequence                                  | result                         |
      | Approval required| A coordinator reviews each request           | one Pending request            |
      | Direct claim     | The first eligible volunteer is confirmed    | one Confirmed assignment       |

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Concurrent direct claims have one winner
    Given an open Direct claim slot
    When two eligible volunteers submit in separate PostgreSQL transactions
    Then one Confirmed assignment, capability, intent, and audit commit
    And the other sees This commitment was just claimed. Choose another opening.
    And the loser persists no volunteer, request, assignment, capability, intent, or audit state

  @SCN003
  Scenario Outline: Recurring policy creates a finite cadence
    Given a published recurring series has generated concrete occurrences
    And a volunteer selects one role, first occurrence, and 12-week horizon
    When the volunteer submits under <policy>
    Then exact Included and Skipped dates were previewed
    And the system creates <initial>
    And no filled, manual, Needs review, or Skipped occurrence is overwritten

    Examples:
      | policy            | initial                                                        |
      | Direct claim      | an Active commitment with Confirmed eligible assignments       |
      | Approval required | one Pending recurring request without a slot reservation       |

  @SCN004
  Scenario: One confirmation accepts an approved cadence
    Given a coordinator approves an approval-required recurring request
    And eligible concrete assignments are Assigned
    When the volunteer confirms through the recurring hub
    Then every still-eligible cadence assignment becomes Confirmed atomically
    And the recurring commitment becomes Active
    And no weekly confirmation is required
    And replay changes nothing

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Volunteer withdraws from a future occurrence
    Given an Active recurring commitment has earlier and later assignments
    When the volunteer confirms withdrawal effective from a selected future occurrence
    Then later cadence assignments are cancelled and their access invalidated atomically
    And earlier assignment/history remains unchanged
    And future slots reopen in coverage
    And replay changes nothing

  @SCN006
  Scenario: One substitute does not end the cadence
    Given a recurring volunteer is assigned across several occurrences
    When a coordinator replaces only one occurrence
    Then that occurrence is marked Replaced and remains an exception
    And the substitute is authoritative for that occurrence
    And the recurring volunteer remains assigned to every other eligible occurrence

  @SCN007
  Scenario: Series revision requires explicit recurring handoff
    Given issue 20 preserves old protected recurring assignments as exceptions after a revision
    When the coordinator previews moving one recurring commitment to revised occurrences
    Then old cancellations, new assignments, skipped conflicts, local changes, access, and messages are listed
    When any mapped target changes before confirmation
    Then no handoff mutation commits
    When the fresh mapping is confirmed
    Then only the selected future set moves atomically and earlier history remains
